WHY THE SPLIT. The panel is a curated dataset rather than software, and MIT fits
data awkwardly. CC BY also makes attribution a licence term rather than a hope,
which is the point: the panel's value is the curation, and citation is how that
is repaid.

UPSTREAM SOURCES are not redistributed here. The build scripts download NCBIfam
(public domain), Pfam (CC0) and Rhea (CC BY 4.0) directly from their providers,
so no upstream licence propagates into this repository. Accessions listed in the
panel are facts about those databases, not copies of them.
